# The deid image builds from the repo root (it needs the `deid` package), so the
# context is the whole tree unless it is excluded here. Everything the image
# actually needs is listed in images/deid/Dockerfile: deid/pyproject.toml,
# deid/uv.lock, deid/src and images/deid/entrypoint.sh.
#
# images/connect builds with its own directory as the context and is unaffected.

.git
.github
*.md
!deid/**/*.md

# Charts, and the policy they mount. The policy is deliberately not in the image.
charts
deid/policy

# Other components.
loadgen
spikes
hack
scripts

# Local artifacts. A .venv copied into the context would be both large and wrong
# for the image's platform.
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.hypothesis
**/.ruff_cache
**/.mypy_cache
deid/tests
